# A room with limits, from the console (TASK-26 Q6a; ADR-0266, ADR-0269): the
# six words in the line, `room set`, `grants`' limits line, the quota hint
# and the keeper's refusal of a limit above the session's. The console's
# shell enters the room through the room keeper, so its lines run in the
# room's one job and a hog in it is refused at the room's memory.
! panicked
! storage failed
< Type help to begin
< \r\n~> 
> room new agent-1 --mem 64M --cpu 25% --procs 16 +w /t/w\r
< agent-1 --colour 1 --mem 64M --cpu 25% --procs 16 +w /t/w
< \r\n~> 
> room\r
< agent-1  --mem 64M --cpu 25% --procs 16  +w /t/w
< \r\n~> 
# --tmp is for untrusted rooms only; an untrusted room is refused for now.
> room set agent-1 --tmp 1M\r
< --tmp is for untrusted rooms only
< \r\n~> 
> room new agent-2 --untrusted +w /t/w\r
< untrusted rooms wait for quotas
< \r\n~> 
# Entering the room: the keeper gives the shell a launch job.
> room agent-1\r
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 64M --cpu 25% --procs 16  (room agent-1)
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# A hog takes all 64M and is refused (OverQuota); the shell says so once.
> memhog\r
< memhog: refused after
< hint: room agent-1 is at its memory limit of 64M; room set agent-1 --mem 128M
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# The next line is refused again: a new hint for the new line, still one.
> memhog\r
< hint: room agent-1 is at its memory limit of 64M
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# top (ADR-0267, INV-0267-1): the room's row against its limits, what refused
# and the line that raises it, from the same reading as the desktop's card;
# `room` shows the use after each limit.
> top\r
< ROOM
< agent-1
< of 64M
< of 16
< (refused
< session
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> top agent-1\r
< limits --mem 64M --cpu 25% --procs 16
< raise: room set agent-1 --mem 128M
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> top nosuch\r
< no such room
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> room\r
< --mem 64M (
< --cpu 25% (
< --procs 16 (
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# The room's job takes the new limit at once.
> room set agent-1 --mem 68M\r
< agent-1 --colour 1 --mem 68M --cpu 25% --procs 16 +w /t/w
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 68M --cpu 25% --procs 16  (room agent-1)
< agent-1 /t/w> 
# Above the session's ceiling: the keeper refuses, the line is put back.
> room set agent-1 --mem 90G\r
< --mem 90G: above the session's
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> grants probe\r
< limits --mem 68M --cpu 25% --procs 16  (room agent-1)
< agent-1 /t/w> 
> room --leave\r
< /t/w> 
> room remove agent-1 --kill\r
< /t/w> 
> room\r
< home
< /t/w> 
> poweroff\r
